.claude/

# Raw US-align output trees: one *_scores.csv / *_cc.csv / *_transform.txt per PAIR, so they grow
# with the square of the instance count (PDB-CPX-137391 alone is 157MB, 154652 is 57MB, ~360MB in
# total). They are INPUTS to scripts/build_instance_similarity.py, not inputs to the site: the
# deploy builds from data/processed/, which holds the finished JSON and the superposed CIFs.
# Leading slash anchors this to the repo root. Unanchored it also matches
# data/processed/PDB-CPX-*/, which is exactly what the deploy builds from.
/PDB-CPX-*/

# one-off spike output, not read by the pipeline or the app
spike_zernike.txt

# session scratch logs
scratch_logs/

# 190MB bond-level intermediate — regenerable by run_batch, not read by the app
data/processed/processed_antibody_antigen_interfaces.json

# external data (Raybould et al. NAR 2021), re-downloadable
paper/covabdab.csv

# Internal spec + paper — kept local, not published to the public repo
spec_revised.md
paper/
# Internal PDBe design documents. Same rule as the spec: this repo serves a public GitHub Pages
# demo, so these stay on disk and out of history.
*.pdf
